## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a real-time moderation workflow with multi-tool planning, guardrails, and production observability on large platforms like Coinbase or Discord.

## Key Concepts

- LangChain agent orchestration with AutoGen planning
- Real-time event streams, idempotency, and dedup
- Tool integration and conditional workflows (SentimentAPI, RiskScoreAPI, ModerationTool)
- Observability, privacy, rate limits, and fault tolerance

## Code Example

```javascript
// high-level skeleton illustrating the planner invocation and routing
async function handleDiscordEvent(evt){
  const plan = await autoGenPlan({event: evt});
  for(const step of plan.steps){
    await executeTool(step.tool, step.args);
  }
  logOutcome(evt.id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the latency budgets under burst traffic?
- How would you recover from partial tool failures without data loss?

