## Why This Is Asked
Understanding cross-language adapter strategies with strict latency and memory constraints.

## Key Concepts
- PEFT vs full fine-tuning in multi-language QA
- Adapter injection points (attention vs MLP)
- Language tagging vs per-language adapters
- Latency/memory budgeting and rollback plans

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo adapter injection sketch
function attachAdapters(model, keys) {
  for (const m of model.modules()) {
    if (m instanceof AttentionLayer || m instanceof MLP) {
      m.addAdapter({rank: 8, name: keys.next()});
    }
  }
  return model;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor drift between languages post-deployment?
- What failure modes require bypassing adapters and using base model instead?

